  "content": {
    "id": "p34-q8-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "What is the largest two-digit number written in base 6? Convert this into decimal form. Why did you expect this number?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$55_6 = 35_{10}$.\n\nThis is one less than $6^2 = 36$, the smallest three-digit number in base 6.",
      "worked": "The largest digit in base 6 is 5, so the largest two-digit number is $55_6$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}55_6 &= 5\\times6+5\\times1\\\\55_6 &= 35_{10}.\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe next number is $100_6 = 6^2 = 36_{10}$, so the largest two-digit number is one less: $35_{10}$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 44
  },
